          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. Write one equation each for decomposition reactions where energy is supplied in the form of heat, light or electricity.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.132,
            0.868,
            0.167
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. What is the difference between displacement and double displacement reactions? Write equations for these reactions.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.168,
            0.868,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14. In the refining of silver, the recovery of silver from silver nitrate solution involved displacement by copper metal. Write down the reaction involved.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.205,
            0.821,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "15. What do you mean by a precipitation reaction? Explain by giving examples.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.224,
            0.853,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "16. Explain the following in terms of gain or loss of oxygen with two examples each. (a) Oxidation",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.264,
            0.299,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Reduction",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.283,
            0.866,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "17. A shiny brown coloured element ‘X’ on heating in air becomes black in colour. Name the element ‘X’ and the black coloured compound formed.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.32,
            0.509,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "18. Why do we apply paint on iron articles?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.34,
            0.729,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "19. Oil and fat containing food items are flushed with nitrogen. Why?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.36,
            0.607,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "20. Explain the following terms with one example each.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.38,
            0.295,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Corrosion",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.4,
            0.292,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Rancidity",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.452,
            0.434,
            0.481
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Group Activity"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.496,
            0.378,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Perform the following activity.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.516,
            0.609,
            0.533
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Take four beakers and label them as A, B, C and D."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.536,
            0.864,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Put 25 mL of water in A, B and C beakers and copper sulphate solution in beaker D.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.556,
            0.865,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Measure and record the temperature of each liquid contained in the beakers above.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.576,
            0.866,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Add two spatulas of potassium sulphate, ammonium nitrate, anhydrous copper "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "sulphate and fine iron fillings to beakers A, B, C and D respectively and stir.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.611,
            0.803,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "n "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Finally measure and record the temperature of each of the mixture above.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.631,
            0.852,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find out which reactions are exothermic and which ones are endothermic in nature.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
